AB  - The differential index, which describes the short-term component of fetal heart rate variability and maternal blood glucose levels were measured 109 times in 19 insulin-dependent diabetic mothers in the 2nd half of gestation. An abnormal differential index was observed more often with maternal hyperglycemia (11/45) than with normoglycemia (5/64). A significant negative linear correlation was found between the differential index and the blood glucose level of the mother.
